// lhdtrack_cfg -- comptime configuration shared by the lhdtrack Pyrope sources.
//
// CONVENTION: the `no_loop` switch
//
// A source whose rolled `for` loop was once rewritten loop-free (unrolled lanes,
// whole-word masks, log-step scans) keeps BOTH forms, and `no_loop` picks one:
//
//   const cfg = import("lhdtrack_cfg")    // file scope, next to the other imports
//
//   pub comb f(...) -> (...) {
//     comptime const W = ...               // declarations both forms use stay outside
//     if cfg.no_loop {
//       ...                                // loop-free form
//     } else {
//       ...                                // loop form (the rolled `for`)
//     }
//   }
//
// Wrap only the statements that differ; ports, registers and shared comptime
// constants stay outside the `if`. Helper lambdas only the loop-free form calls
// stay at file scope: uncalled, they are never instantiated, and with an
// explicit --top lhd does not even lower or emit an uncalled non-pub comb, so
// the switch leaves no trace in the netlist or the emitted Verilog.
//
// Only sources whose loops were removed by an edit carry the switch. The loop
// form is the idiomatic Pyrope this corpus measures; the loop-free form is the
// hand-tuned reference, kept so the tests where the loop synthesizes worse
// remain a benchmark for future LiveHD work. Some loops are not worse, and that
// is fine. Do not add a loop-free alternative to any other loop.
//
// HOW lhd FINDS THIS FILE. `import("x")` resolves only to x.prp in the
// importing file's own directory (no search path, no ancestor fallback), so
// every test that imports it carries a RELATIVE symlink:
//
//   ln -s ../../common/lhdtrack_cfg.prp tests/<t>/pyrope/lhdtrack_cfg.prp
//
// The link also makes the flows see the shared value: the lhdtrack cache key
// hashes tests/<t>/pyrope/* through the link (corpus.Test.source_files), and
// sim_lhd_pyrope's copy of pyrope/*.prp follows it. lhd's own incremental
// compile cache keys the imported file's content as well.
//
// ZERO QoR IMPACT. `no_loop` is comptime: upass folds the `if` and drops the
// dead branch before any hardware exists, like a preprocessor #if. With
// no_loop=false a converted source emits the same netlist as the pure loop
// source, with no_loop=true the same as the pure loop-free source. Any
// difference is a LiveHD bug, not a property of the test.
//
// FLIPPING IT. Default false: the corpus measures the loop forms. For a
// loop-free benchmark run set `no_loop = true` here (or in a private copy of
// the tree) and run as usual; every converted test re-keys and re-measures.
// Committing a flipped value changes the measured circuit of every converted
// test -- call it out like a baseline recipe change.
pub comptime const no_loop = false
